A compact notation for the field is: $\mathcal{V}
=
\{\text{war},\ \text{killing},\ \text{aggression},\ \text{competition},\ \text{becoming},\ \text{suppression},\ \text{resistance}\}.$ Here $\mathcal{V}$ is not a formal set in a technical theory. It is a reader’s shorthand for the range Krishnamurti opens before asking whether we will look at violence bit by bit or as a whole.

